    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d791">

                <pb facs="0838" n="826" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg826"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 (D) E.D.B./2261: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-01-25T00:00:00-04:00">January 25,
                        1943—midnight.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>91. Since the receipt of your telegram no. 18, January 5, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="73"
                        xml:id="d791-f1"/> the Department and other agencies of this Government have
                    been <pb facs="0839" n="827" xml:id="pg827"/> awaiting anxiously word from you
                    that the negotiations looking to the limitation of Chilean consumption of copper
                    for manufacture and export had been satisfactorily concluded. The Reconstruction
                    Finance Corporation has pointed out that exports of copper and copper
                    manufactures are now exceeding the 20,000–ton annual goal by approximately 1,000
                    tons per month. This is a serious loss to United Nations military requirements
                    and further delay in arriving at an agreement can bring only detriment in the
                    prosecution of the war. Please immediately present this case forcefully to the
                    appropriate authorities and spare no effort to follow the negotiation through to
                    a prompt and satisfactory conclusion within the framework we have already set
                    up.</p>
                <p>The Department again repeats the seriousness of this situation. Please reply by
                    telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d791-f1" n="73" xml:id="d791-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it indicated that Chile was about to issue a decree controlling the
                    domestic consumption of copper.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
